# Metadata is the index

When you need to group, categorize, filter, or order anything in this repo — pages, papers, code
chunks, diagrams, notes — the answer is **a field on the object**, read at runtime. Never a constant
list of ids inside a component, and never a category that exists only as a heading in prose.

Before writing a grouping, read `content/CONTROL.md` → "Metadata is the index (standing law)" and
`data/docs/metadata-law.md` (`/docs/metadata-law`).

The four steps:

1. Add a field named for the question it answers.
2. Give it a derivation default so objects already on disk classify with no migration.
3. Parse it into the record type so it reaches `GET /api/*`. An unparsed key is decoration.
4. Group by reading the field. A component may own labels and display order, never membership.

Metadata surfaces: page YAML frontmatter (`data/md/`, `data/docs/`), paper headers
(`data/papers/<id>.md`), `# @chunk` comment fences, `data/diagrams/*.json`.

If you catch yourself typing an array of ids to make a section appear, stop and add the field.
